        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f72305ba-02b8-534c-af68-0d4fc6253caf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Rescuers, The Muppets, The Fox and the Hound, Macbeth, Muppets Most Wanted, Alice Through the Looking Glass\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions, Buena Vista Distribution\n- People: Jeanette Nolan, James Bobin\n- Topics: film genres, voice roles, release dates, directing credits\n\nFacts:\n- Macbeth is a 1948 film in which Jeanette Nolan had a role.\n- Jeanette Nolan is best known for roles in the television series The Virginian from 1962 to 1971 and Dirty Sally in 1974.\n- The Rescuers is a 1977 American animated comedy-drama adventure film produced by Walt Disney Productions.\n- The Rescuers was first released on June 22, 1977, by Buena Vista Distribution.\n- Jeanette Nolan voiced Ellie Mae in the 1977 Disney animated film The Rescuers.\n- Jeanette Nolan voiced Widow Tweed in the 1981 Disney animated film The Fox and the Hound.\n- The Muppets is a 2011 American musical comedy film and the seventh theatrical film featuring the Muppets.\n- James Bobin directed The Muppets in 2011, Muppets Most Wanted in 2014, and Alice Through the Looking Glass in 2016.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "512ad8d7-6810-5fdf-8ee5-f289acd062b7",
        "text": "Page: The Rescuers. Sentence: The Rescuers is a 1977 American animated comedy-drama adventure film produced by Walt Disney Productions and first released on June 22, 1977, by Buena Vista Distribution.\nPage: The Muppets (film). Sentence: The Muppets is a 2011 American musical comedy film and the seventh theatrical film featuring the Muppets.\nPage: Jeanette Nolan. Sentence: She is best known for her roles in the television series \"The Virginian\" (1962 - 1971) and \"Dirty Sally\" (1974); and in films such as \"Macbeth\" (1948) and as the voices of Ellie Mae and Widow Tweed in the animated Disney films, \"The Rescuers\" (1977) and \"The Fox and the Hound\" (1981) respectively.\nPage: James Bobin. Sentence: He directed the feature films \"The Muppets\" (2011), \"Muppets Most Wanted\" (2014) and \"Alice Through the Looking Glass\" (2016).",
